# Declarative Go packages to cross-compile for all arches in B19_GO_CROSS_ARCHES.
# Format: <package@version> (one per line)
# Binary name is derived from the package path (last component before @).
# Output: ${GOBIN}/<binary>.<arch> (e.g. dasel.amd64, dasel.arm64, dasel.riscv64).
# Used to break OS-layer bootstrap cycles — downstream consumers pick the right arch binary.

# Example: cross-compile dasel for amd64, arm64, riscv64
# github.com/tomwright/dasel/v2/cmd/dasel@v2.8.0

# Example: cross-compile yq for all supported arches
# github.com/mikefarah/yq/v4@latest

# Example: cross-compile a custom tool
# github.com/example/mytool/cmd/mytool@v1.0.0